  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Preheat the oven to 220C. Line a oven tray with baking paper. Crush or finely chop 1 garlic clove. Halve the cherry tomatoes. Rinse and drain the chickpeas.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/68694/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_01-3c5e09c19014ea60abcdf05ac61091d4.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make topping: Put the chickpeas, 1 tbs Indian masala spice blend (see cooking tip), half the yoghurt and half the garlic in a bowl, season with salt and pepper and stir well to coat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/68695/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_02-2926580d9bbc8c56d65fa9aea6b809f9.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make garlic yoghurt: Combine the remaining yoghurt and garlic in a separate bowl, season with salt and pepper, then spread over the naan, leaving a 2cm border. Reserve any remainder to serve.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/68696/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_03-a49ec27f5bf99ddf4ba0511d16af9859.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake pizzas: Transfer the naan to the lined tray and top with the chickpea mixture and tomatoes. Drizzle with 2 tsp olive oil and season with salt and pepper. Bake for 10 mins or until the bases are golden and the tomatoes are soft.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/68697/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_04-bc759d4f4e2c78354fd94ba1a59b85a9.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Meanwhile, put the spinach in a medium frypan over medium heat and stir-fry for 1-2 mins until wilted. Top the pizzas with the wilted spinach, dollop over any remaining garlic yoghurt and season with salt and pepper to serve.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/68698/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_05-5a7a1690f603c65ff6737795493d279d.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen hack: To make your yoghurt a drizzling consistency, add a little cold water and stir to combine. For a nice crisp pizza base, put the oven tray in the oven while preheating, then put the uncooked pizzas on the hot tray.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/68699/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_HACK-4d24763fbe97269c0089cc30f420a7fa.jpg"
    }
  ]
}
